---
title: Oatmeal raisin cookies
servings: 48
yield: 4 dozen cookies
tags: [american, vegetarian]
cuisine: american
time: 44 minutes
source: The Best Oatmeal Raisin Cookies by Elise Bauer, Simply Recipes, https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/oatmeal_raisin_cookies/
---

Heat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Grease or line two large #baking sheets{}.

Beat the @unsalted butter{1%cup}(softened) in a #large bowl{} until creamy. Add
the @brown sugar{1%cup}(packed, light or dark) and
@granulated sugar{10%tbsp}(1/2 cup plus 2 tbsp) and beat ~{3%minutes} until
fluffy.

Beat in the @eggs{2}, one at a time, then the @vanilla extract{1%tbsp}.

In a #medium bowl{}, mix the @all-purpose flour{1.5%cup}, @kosher salt{3/4%tsp},
@baking soda{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1%tsp} and
@nutmeg{1/2%tsp}(freshly grated). Stir this into the butter mixture.

Stir in the @raisins{1.5%cup} and @walnuts{1/2%cup}(chopped, optional), then the
@rolled oats{3%cup}.

Drop large tablespoons of dough onto the sheets, at least 2 inches apart. Bake
~{10%minutes} to 12 minutes, until the edges are golden, swapping the sheets
halfway if baking two at once.

Leave on the sheets ~{1%minute}, then move to a #wire rack{} to cool completely.

> They look underdone everywhere but the edges when they come out. They firm
> up as they cool. Old-fashioned or quick oats both work; instant does not.
